---
import TutorialLayout from '../../layouts/TutorialLayout.astro';

const cardClass = "group p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-border hover:border-accent/40 transition-colors";
const cardTitleClass = "font-semibold text-text group-hover:text-accent transition-colors";
const cardDescClass = "text-sm text-text-muted mt-1";
---

<TutorialLayout
  title="Tutorials"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Tutorials' },
  ]}
>
  <p class="text-text-muted text-lg mb-12 leading-relaxed">
    A progressive learning path showcasing Rumoca's features, from your first Modelica model to model predictive control for a drone.
    Each tutorial builds on the last, and they all run in your browser via WebAssembly.
  </p>

  <div class="space-y-12">
    <section>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-accent bg-accent/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">1</span>
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text hover:text-accent transition-colors">Getting Started</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-6">Write Modelica, compile, simulate, and plot &mdash; the full workflow from the start.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started/first-model" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Your First Model</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>The simplest second-order ODE. Constant acceleration.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started/mass-spring-damper" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Mass-Spring-Damper</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Linear second-order ODE. Compare compilation backends.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started/bouncing-ball" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Bouncing Ball</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Event handling with <code class="font-mono text-xs">when</code> clauses.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started/van-der-pol" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Van der Pol Oscillator</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Limit cycles and solver settings.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started/series-rlc" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Series RLC Circuit</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Underdamped oscillation. Parameter exploration.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/getting-started/circuit-components" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Circuit Components</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Component-based Modelica with connectors and inheritance.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-accent bg-accent/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">2</span>
        <a href="/tutorials/visualization" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text hover:text-accent transition-colors">3D Visualization</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-6">Bring your models to life with interactive Three.js scenes.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/tutorials/visualization/bouncing-ball-3d" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Bouncing Ball 3D</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Your first 3D viewer. The <code class="font-mono text-xs">onInit</code>/<code class="font-mono text-xs">onFrame</code> API.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/visualization/two-body-orbit" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Two-Body Orbit</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Orbital mechanics with trail rendering.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/visualization/pendulum" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Pendulum</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Nonlinear pendulum dynamics with 3D visualization.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-accent bg-accent/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">3</span>
        <a href="/tutorials/workflows" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text hover:text-accent transition-colors">Code Generation Workflows</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-6">Modelica in, any language out &mdash; CasADi for optimization, SymPy for analysis, FMU for co-simulation.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/tutorials/workflows/casadi" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Simulation with CasADi</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Compile to CasADi and simulate with Python.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/workflows/sympy-bode" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>SymPy &amp; Bode Plots</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Symbolic analysis and frequency-domain plots.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/workflows/custom-templates" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Custom Jinja Templates</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Generate MATLAB, Fortran, C, or any format.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/workflows/fmu-export" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>FMU Export for MATLAB</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Export FMUs and import into Simulink.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-accent bg-accent/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">4</span>
        <a href="/tutorials/controls" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text hover:text-accent transition-colors">Control Systems</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-6">Close the loop &mdash; from a DC motor to a flying quadrotor.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/tutorials/controls/dc-motor-pid" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>PID DC Motor</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Closed-loop PID control end to end.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/controls/pendulum-on-cart" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Pendulum on Cart</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Coupled DAE system with constraint forces.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/controls/quadrotor" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Quadrotor Autopilot</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>6-DOF quaternion dynamics with cascaded control.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-accent bg-accent/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">5</span>
        <a href="/tutorials/optimization" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text hover:text-accent transition-colors">Optimization &amp; MPC</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-6">The real power &mdash; Modelica dynamics go straight into CasADi for trajectory optimization and MPC.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/tutorials/optimization/optimal-control" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Optimal Control Intro</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Your first trajectory optimization with CasADi.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/optimization/pendulum-swingup" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>Pendulum Swing-Up</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Full swing-up trajectory via direct transcription.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/optimization/mpc-quadrotor" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>MPC: Quadrotor</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>Receding-horizon MPC for quadrotor hover.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutorials/optimization/mpc-fixed-wing" class={cardClass}>
          <h3 class={cardTitleClass}>MPC: Fixed-Wing Aircraft</h3>
          <p class={cardDescClass}>MPC path following for a SportCub airplane.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</TutorialLayout>
